                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-variables" Title="CSS variables" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Vars.Length, "variables")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssVariables" Title="CSS variables" Rows="Vocab.Vars" />
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li>Panel collapse tabs are native buttons titled "Collapse panel" / "Expand panel"; their only text is an arrow glyph.</li>
            <li>The splitter bar is a native button with <code>role="separator"</code>, <code>aria-orientation</code> and the <code>Title</code> as its name. Arrow keys move it by <code>KeyboardStep</code>, Home and End go to the limits, double-click resets.</li>
            <li>The splitter imports the library's own <code>splitter-control.js</code> for the drag guide and measuring. No third-party script. Page layout and dashboard are CSS only.</li>
            <li>Dashboard panels are plain grid items with no landmarks or headings of their own; give each panel's content a heading.</li>
            <li>Grid and stack layouts render a plain <code>div</code> with inline styles, no role and no script. Screen readers follow source order, so write cells in reading order rather than reordering them with <code>Column</code> and <code>Row</code>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Dockable, floating panes: <a href="demo/dock-manager">Dock manager</a>. Keyboard navigation across a page's regions: <a href="demo/page-navigation">Page navigation</a>.</li>
            <li>For the content of a panel: <code>GridLayoutControl</code>, with <code>GridLayoutItemControl</code> for placed and spanning cells, and <code>StackLayoutControl</code> are shown in <a href="demo/layout#grid">Grid and stack layouts</a> above.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

